2. Experimental system
The experimental apparatus used in this study is depicted in Fig. 2 (a). Due to the limited space and small diameter, as well as the symmetry of the elliptical tube, two rows of seven thermocouple wires are carefully soldered onto both the top and side walls. These wires are evenly distributed to measure the wall temperature, as depicted in Fig. 2 (b). The bulk temperature of the working fluid is measured using two Ktype armored thermocouples at the entrance and exit of the experimental AM elliptical channels.
